    {
        "id": "63edc8169582e3b8",
        "type": "function",
        "z": "1c00011a6f22edfe",
        "name": "msg type 05,03,03 motor 2",
        "func": "var sequence = [5, 3, 3];\n/*\nWe can now clearly see the Polling Cycle of your Master controller. It iterates through the slave IDs requesting specific blocks of data.\n\n    Step 1: Ask Device 4 for Registers 1011–1024.\n\n    Step 2: (Wait for reply).\n\n    Step 3: Ask Device 5 for Registers 1011–1024. ← (You are here)\n    */\n\n\nif (msg.payload) {\n    var isMatch = true;\n\n    for (var i = 0; i < sequence.length; i++) {\n        if (msg.payload[i] !== sequence[i]) {\n            isMatch = false;\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (isMatch) {\n        // The message starts with the specified sequence\n        // You can perform further actions or send the message to the next node\n        return msg;\n    }\n}\n\n// The message does not start with the specified sequence\n// You can choose to discard the message or send it to a different node\nreturn null;",
        "outputs": 1,
        "timeout": "",
