    {
        "id": "e0f029733448eeeb",
        "type": "function",
        "z": "1c00011a6f22edfe",
        "name": "msg type 02,03,11 Display 2",
        "func": "var sequence = [2, 3, 11];\n/*\nFirst Msg: [1, 3, 11, 185, 0, 21...] (Ask Device 1 for registers 3001-3021)\n\n    This Msg: [2, 3, 11, 185, 0, 21...] (Ask Device 2 for registers 3001-3021)\n\nConclusion: Your Master Controller is Polling. It is looping through its list of devices (Device 1, then Device 2, likely followed by Device 3...) asking them all for the exact same block of data (registers 3001 to 3021).\n    */\n\n\nif (msg.payload) {\n    var isMatch = true;\n\n    for (var i = 0; i < sequence.length; i++) {\n        if (msg.payload[i] !== sequence[i]) {\n            isMatch = false;\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (isMatch) {\n        // The message starts with the specified sequence\n        // You can perform further actions or send the message to the next node\n        return msg;\n    }\n}\n\n// The message does not start with the specified sequence\n// You can choose to discard the message or send it to a different node\nreturn null;",
